{"name":"Sunday Sky","hex":"#c5d2d5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunday","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday is the day of the week between Saturday and Monday. Sunday is a day of rest in most Western countries and a part of the weekend. In some Arab countries, Sunday is a weekday."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday","wikidata":"Q132"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sol Iustitiae (Sun of Righteousness), derived from the Judeo-Christian Bible, Malachi 4:2. By Albrecht Dürer, c. 1499/1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APierre-Le-Moyne-De-l'art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/M%C3%A1ni_and_S%C3%B3l_by_Lorenz_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-M%C3%A1ni_and_S%C3%B3l_by_Lorenz_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/M%C3%A1ni_and_S%C3%B3l_by_Lorenz_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-M%C3%A1ni_and_S%C3%B3l_by_Lorenz_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A depiction of Máni, the personified Moon, and his sister Sól, the personified Sun, from Norse mythology (1895) by Lorenz Frølich